+## Failed session initialization
+
+- When `beforeSession` throws an `Error`, the caller receives the same rejection after `onError(session, error)` and `afterSession(session)` have been awaited in that order, each once with the original session (and original error for `onError`), provided those hooks complete normally; no user-input or model processing happens, and cleanup must tolerate initialization that allocated nothing or only partially completed, using deployer-owned allocation state rather than assuming the turn started ([validated by: reports and cleans up a failed beforeSession before rejecting with the original error](../../src/orchestration/beforeSession.acceptance.test.ts#L7)).
